WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.140
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.410 --> 01:34.900
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.270 --> 01:37.840
[Episode 24]

4
01:41.310 --> 01:42.970
Regiment Commander, I have a request.

5
01:42.970 --> 01:43.640
Go ahead.

6
01:44.200 --> 01:45.259
I can't speak for the others,

7
01:45.259 --> 01:47.500
If I, Mao Zhenhua, capture the highest-ranking one,

8
01:47.500 --> 01:49.759
can you give me your revolver as a reward?

9
01:57.420 --> 02:00.080
If you don't want to give it to me, forget I asked.

10
02:02.790 --> 02:03.460
Deal.

11
02:04.080 --> 02:05.140
Anything else?

12
02:05.230 --> 02:06.410
-No more! -That's all!

13
02:06.410 --> 02:07.130
Move out.

14
02:07.860 --> 02:09.419
Let's go! Come on!

15
02:12.620 --> 02:13.500
Tang Yunshan!

16
02:12.670 --> 02:15.700
[Zhongzhuangpu, Guizhou]

17
02:13.800 --> 02:15.830
Throw all the troops you have into the fight!

18
02:15.830 --> 02:16.800
If we can't take Laoyashan,

19
02:15.860 --> 02:19.320
[Wu Qiwei, Commander of the 1st Column, 2nd Route Army of the KMT Troops' Pursuit Army]

20
02:17.120 --> 02:18.190
neither of us will be able to

21
02:18.190 --> 02:19.870
answer to Commander-in-Chief Xue!

22
02:19.870 --> 02:21.520
It's not that I'm not giving it my all,

23
02:21.520 --> 02:23.210
but I really can't hold out much longer!

24
02:23.210 --> 02:25.630
Those Communist soldiers are like crazy on the battlefield!

25
02:25.630 --> 02:26.910
They charge straight in our clusters

26
02:26.910 --> 02:29.470
with bundles of grenades in their arms!

27
02:32.910 --> 02:33.570
Commander!

28
02:33.800 --> 02:35.030
Commander! Bad news!

29
02:36.280 --> 02:38.680
The Communist Army is attacking from the north!

30
02:38.680 --> 02:39.930
How many men do they have?

31
02:39.930 --> 02:41.730
They're all over the mountains!

32
02:41.730 --> 02:42.710
The north?

33
02:44.890 --> 02:46.710
Weren't Wang Jialie's two regiments stationed there?

34
02:46.710 --> 02:47.030
Yes.

35
02:47.050 --> 02:48.310
They've already fled!

36
02:48.490 --> 02:50.150
The retreating Guizhou troops say

37
02:50.150 --> 02:52.560
Wang Jialie has probably reached Xinchang by now.

38
02:52.560 --> 02:53.610
Damn Wang Jialie!

39
03:04.300 --> 03:05.900
Commander! Commander!

40
03:06.670 --> 03:07.760
We should retreat now,

41
03:07.760 --> 03:09.550
or it will be too late!

42
03:13.620 --> 03:14.410
Retreat.

43
03:15.690 --> 03:16.280
Retreat!

44
03:16.400 --> 03:17.260
Hurry! Retreat!

45
03:17.260 --> 03:18.030
Retreat!

46
03:18.490 --> 03:18.980
Good.

47
03:20.350 --> 03:22.079
Zhongzhuangpu has been taken.

48
03:22.340 --> 03:25.400
The Kuomintang Central Army is retreating south across the entire front!

49
03:25.400 --> 03:27.120
Order the Second Division to pursue them

50
03:27.120 --> 03:27.650
at full speed.

51
03:27.650 --> 03:28.220
How far?

52
03:28.870 --> 03:29.930
Fifty kilometers.

53
03:30.430 --> 03:31.430
All the way

54
03:35.030 --> 03:36.230
to the Wujiang River.

55
03:55.220 --> 03:55.950
Pursue them.

56
03:56.570 --> 03:58.370
All the way to the Wujiang River.

57
03:58.500 --> 04:00.410
From last October to today,

58
04:00.740 --> 04:03.340
after four months of pursuit

59
04:03.360 --> 04:05.640
by the KMT troops, the Central Red Army

60
04:05.670 --> 04:06.880
finally won

61
04:06.900 --> 04:09.060
a stunning turnaround battle today.

62
04:09.550 --> 04:10.280
Pursue them!

63
04:10.460 --> 04:12.260
All the way to the Wujiang River.

64
04:12.290 --> 04:14.040
The Red Army's advance is unstoppable!

65
04:14.040 --> 04:16.370
Today, we can finally hold our heads high!

66
04:16.980 --> 04:17.709
Pursue them!

67
04:18.180 --> 04:19.950
All the way to the Wujiang River.

68
04:19.950 --> 04:22.070
Make the enemy abandon their weapons and equipment as they flee.

69
04:22.070 --> 04:24.670
The Red Army's battle cries terrify the enemy.

70
04:24.910 --> 04:26.400
Pursue them all the way to the Wujiang River.

71
04:26.400 --> 04:28.320
The tables have turned!

72
04:28.530 --> 04:31.730
We've finally seized the initiative on the battlefield!

73
04:37.120 --> 04:37.920
Don't move!

74
04:38.550 --> 04:39.430
Get down!

75
04:46.590 --> 04:48.320
Get down! Don't move! Get down!

76
04:48.400 --> 04:49.320
Don't move!

77
04:58.760 --> 04:59.710
Drop your weapons and you'll be spared!

78
04:59.710 --> 05:00.600
Put them down!

79
05:01.950 --> 05:03.190
Hand over your guns! Now!

80
05:03.190 --> 05:04.650
We will hand over our guns.

81
05:28.440 --> 05:29.150
Don't move!

82
05:32.670 --> 05:33.360
Hands up!

83
05:35.640 --> 05:36.840
Hands up. Don't move!

84
05:37.140 --> 05:38.470
Comrades, don't shoot!

85
05:38.570 --> 05:40.159
We surrender! We surrender!

86
05:40.159 --> 05:41.830
You are the Central Army after all.

87
05:41.830 --> 05:43.960
Even the way you surrender is orderly.

88
05:45.010 --> 05:45.800
The Red Army is here!

89
05:45.800 --> 05:46.270
Get up!

90
05:49.490 --> 05:50.490
Put your hands up!

91
05:51.520 --> 05:52.750
Name and rank!

92
05:54.909 --> 05:55.550
Hurry up!

93
05:56.600 --> 05:57.190
I...

94
05:57.430 --> 05:58.040
I am...

95
05:58.400 --> 06:01.660
the Chief of Staff of the 59th Division of the Central Army.

96
06:01.790 --> 06:02.430
Company Commander,

97
06:02.430 --> 06:04.310
looks like that commander's revolver will surely be yours.

98
06:04.310 --> 06:05.160
Of course!

99
06:06.350 --> 06:07.790
Don't celebrate just yet.

100
06:07.790 --> 06:10.040
What if another company captures Wu Qiwei?

101
06:10.040 --> 06:11.300
Keep a close eye on him.

102
06:11.600 --> 06:12.190
Let's go!

103
06:12.830 --> 06:13.390
Go!

104
06:22.160 --> 06:23.830
The elite of the Party.

105
06:25.110 --> 06:26.870
The army's finest division.

106
06:46.750 --> 06:50.159
How am I supposed to face the Commander-in-Chief after this?

107
06:50.159 --> 06:50.560
Don't!

108
06:50.560 --> 06:52.020
-Commander! -Commander!

109
06:52.070 --> 06:53.400
Don't do it, Commander.

110
06:54.040 --> 06:54.680
Let go!

111
06:54.700 --> 06:57.140
Commander, the river is just ahead.

112
06:57.440 --> 06:59.040
The pontoon bridge is ready.

113
06:59.750 --> 07:01.750
Quick! Get the commander in the car!

114
07:02.420 --> 07:04.420
Hurry up!

115
07:15.360 --> 07:16.220
Chief of Staff.

116
07:16.570 --> 07:17.480
Yes, sir!

117
07:23.060 --> 07:24.720
Once we've crossed the river,

118
07:25.400 --> 07:26.460
blow up the bridge.

119
07:29.560 --> 07:30.510
Commander.

120
07:30.790 --> 07:32.390
We've still got a lot of men behind us.

121
07:32.390 --> 07:34.590
Our supply unit is still behind us, too.

122
07:37.620 --> 07:38.500
Yes, sir!

123
07:42.440 --> 07:43.390
Go.

124
07:45.250 --> 07:47.570
From February 24

125
07:47.600 --> 07:48.750
to February 28,

126
07:49.240 --> 07:51.570
after crossing the Chishui River for the second time,

127
07:51.570 --> 07:53.370
the Central Red Army has taken

128
07:53.390 --> 07:56.270
Tongzi, Loushanguan, and Zunyi in just five days.

129
07:56.440 --> 07:58.460
It routed and wiped out two divisions

130
07:58.460 --> 08:00.390
and eight regiments of KMT troops,

131
08:00.640 --> 08:03.050
killed or wounded more than 2,400 enemy soldiers,

132
08:03.050 --> 08:04.850
and took around 3,000 captives.

133
08:04.870 --> 08:07.160
Countless weapons and supplies were seized.

134
08:07.160 --> 08:10.930
It was the Red Army's greatest victory since the Long March began,

135
08:11.220 --> 08:13.740
later known as the Great Victory at Zunyi.

136
08:15.910 --> 08:16.630
Gentlemen,

137
08:16.820 --> 08:17.690
during the Battle of Tucheng,

138
08:17.250 --> 08:22.470
[Fan Shaozeng's Residence, Chongqing]

139
08:18.050 --> 08:18.600
the Sichuan Army,

140
08:18.600 --> 08:20.660
under the leadership of Yizhi (Guo Xunqi),

141
08:20.660 --> 08:21.520
fought bravely

142
08:21.770 --> 08:24.010
and sent the Communist army fleeing west in disarray,

143
08:24.010 --> 08:26.340
abandoning their weapons and equipment.

144
08:26.910 --> 08:29.840
Yizhi is truly a role model for the Nationalist Army.

145
08:34.330 --> 08:36.330
I was just doing my duty as a soldier.

146
08:36.390 --> 08:37.950
You flatter me, Generalissimo.

147
08:37.950 --> 08:39.280
Please, have a seat.

148
08:40.010 --> 08:42.270
I never hesitate to praise those who have

149
08:42.350 --> 08:44.049
distinguished themselves in battle,

150
08:44.049 --> 08:46.650
and I hold them in the highest regard.

151
08:47.140 --> 08:48.000
In this battle,

152
08:48.130 --> 08:50.150
the Sichuan Army made a name for itself.

153
08:50.150 --> 08:51.660
They contained the Communist Army from south of the river

154
08:51.660 --> 08:54.180
and prevented them from crossing northward.

155
08:54.180 --> 08:56.940
[Chen Cheng Commander-in-Chief of the Kuomintang Army's Reserve Forces in Jiangxi]

156
08:54.550 --> 08:57.200
They forced them eastward and back into northern Guizhou.

157
08:57.000 --> 09:00.190
[Yan Daogang, Director of the Aide-de-Camp Office of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

158
08:57.510 --> 08:58.770
This shows that the Communist Army

159
08:58.770 --> 09:00.700
is nearing the end of its strength.

160
09:00.780 --> 09:02.450
Now is our best opportunity

161
09:03.030 --> 09:04.830
to destroy them once and for all.

162
09:04.930 --> 09:05.690
Gentlemen.

163
09:06.170 --> 09:08.430
I, Chiang Kai-shek, have come to Sichuan

164
09:08.510 --> 09:11.080
to fight alongside you.

165
09:11.280 --> 09:14.280
I'm determined to secure victory.

166
09:15.450 --> 09:16.450
However, I have

167
09:17.440 --> 09:21.130
one small request

168
09:21.160 --> 09:23.130
of our comrades in the Sichuan Army.

169
09:23.130 --> 09:25.770
You should

170
09:25.790 --> 09:27.160
take a broader view.

171
09:27.290 --> 09:28.810
If your only concern is

172
09:28.840 --> 09:31.290
keeping the Communist Army out of Sichuan,

173
09:31.630 --> 09:32.960
then where does that

174
09:33.280 --> 09:34.610
leave the Party?

175
09:35.150 --> 09:36.870
It is truly unacceptable.

176
09:38.360 --> 09:40.510
So, Yizhi,

177
09:41.100 --> 09:42.230
I'm counting on you.

178
09:45.990 --> 09:46.990
Act vigorously.

179
09:50.500 --> 09:51.420
Act quickly.

180
09:54.470 --> 09:55.500
Act firmly.

181
09:55.970 --> 09:58.830
United in purpose, we shall achieve total victory!

182
09:59.420 --> 10:00.840
Please rest assured, Generalissimo.

183
10:00.840 --> 10:01.710
I will fulfill my duty

184
10:01.710 --> 10:03.440
and take full responsibility.

185
10:15.550 --> 10:17.000
According to reliable intelligence,

186
10:17.000 --> 10:20.780
there has been a major change in the Communist Army since the New Year.

187
10:20.780 --> 10:23.110
The top leadership of the Communist Army has changed,

188
10:23.110 --> 10:25.110
and Mao Zedong has resumed command.

189
10:32.470 --> 10:34.470
What we least wanted to see

190
10:35.000 --> 10:36.120
has happened.

191
10:36.270 --> 10:37.300
This Mao Zedong

192
10:37.670 --> 10:38.910
is really a headache.

193
10:39.250 --> 10:41.470
His military strategy is unpredictable,

194
10:41.470 --> 10:42.800
and he likes to feint in one direction and strikes in another.

195
10:42.800 --> 10:45.400
Our defeat at Zunyi this time is a lesson.

196
10:45.780 --> 10:47.580
The areas around Zunyi are mostly long and narrow,

197
10:47.580 --> 10:50.120
leaving the Communist Army little room to maneuver.

198
10:50.120 --> 10:50.940
Today's loss

199
10:50.970 --> 10:52.880
may turn into tomorrow's gain.

200
10:53.120 --> 10:53.890
That explains it.

201
10:53.890 --> 10:55.420
Since early spring this year,

202
10:55.420 --> 10:57.470
the Communist Army has been behaving very strangely.

203
10:57.470 --> 10:59.470
Mao Zedong went the long way around,

204
11:00.420 --> 11:02.870
but he still wants to face us head-on.

205
11:03.720 --> 11:04.890
But he is different from those

206
11:04.890 --> 11:06.470
who went to Moscow and absorbed

207
11:06.470 --> 11:07.470
foreign culture.

208
11:07.530 --> 11:08.290
The losses

209
11:08.900 --> 11:10.370
we suffered in our previous

210
11:10.370 --> 11:11.700
encirclement campaign

211
11:12.130 --> 11:13.620
are still fresh in our minds.

212
11:13.620 --> 11:14.570
But next time,

213
11:14.900 --> 11:17.760
we won't let him gain even the slightest advantage!

214
11:17.960 --> 11:18.870
Yes, sir!

215
11:19.290 --> 11:24.190
[Zunyi, Guizhou]

216
11:20.570 --> 11:22.450
Comrades, look ahead!

217
11:22.710 --> 11:24.710
Listen as I announce our victories!

218
11:24.780 --> 11:26.850
Just three days after crossing the Chishui River eastward,

219
11:26.850 --> 11:28.910
the Red Army captured Tongzi County.

220
11:28.960 --> 11:30.700
We pushed south with unstoppable momentum,

221
11:30.700 --> 11:32.430
then we captured Loushanguan.

222
11:32.470 --> 11:34.270
The Guizhou Army was terrified.

223
11:34.360 --> 11:36.440
Our fame spread after taking Zunyi for the second time.

224
11:36.440 --> 11:37.860
We drove Wu Qiwei away outside the city,

225
11:37.860 --> 11:40.790
and chased the enemy all the way to the Wujiang River.

226
11:41.150 --> 11:43.840
Bravo!

227
11:43.840 --> 11:45.360
Comrades, look ahead!

228
11:45.570 --> 11:47.390
[Zhu Rui, Director of the Political Department of the 1st Red Army Corps]

229
11:45.630 --> 11:47.630
Listen as I announce our victories!

230
11:47.790 --> 11:49.520
Just three days after crossing the Chishui River eastward...

231
11:49.520 --> 11:50.310
Mao Zhenhua.

232
11:50.780 --> 11:52.310
I heard you caught a big one!

233
11:52.710 --> 11:53.550
It's nothing.

234
11:54.080 --> 11:55.510
It's just a Chief of Staff.

235
11:55.510 --> 11:57.240
You're really something, lad!

236
11:57.870 --> 11:59.790
The bamboo clappers sound loud and clear,

237
11:59.790 --> 12:01.550
let's sing the praises of Company Commander Mao!

238
12:01.550 --> 12:03.550
Company Commander Mao is a real fighter!

239
12:03.550 --> 12:05.200
He chased the enemy all the way to the Wujiang River,

240
12:05.200 --> 12:07.030
and captured their Chief of Staff.

241
12:07.030 --> 12:08.720
His heroic deeds will be sung far and wide,

242
12:08.720 --> 12:10.270
far and wide!

243
12:10.720 --> 12:12.150
Bravo!

244
12:12.170 --> 12:12.810
Bravo!

245
12:13.010 --> 12:13.920
Mr. Luo,

246
12:14.130 --> 12:16.330
don't just praise me with the clappers.

247
12:16.480 --> 12:18.000
The other comrades deserve credit, too.

248
12:18.000 --> 12:18.720
Right?

249
12:18.950 --> 12:19.680
Absolutely!

250
12:19.970 --> 12:20.970
Let's sing a song.

251
12:21.090 --> 12:22.930
Sing a song from the Central Soviet Area.

252
12:22.930 --> 12:23.530
Sure!

253
12:23.550 --> 12:25.420
Company Commander Mao, what would you like to hear?

254
12:25.420 --> 12:28.330
"To Be a Soldier, Join the Red Army!"

255
12:28.600 --> 12:29.480
No problem!

256
12:29.790 --> 12:31.650
To be a soldier, join the Red Army.

257
12:31.720 --> 12:33.360
One, two, three, sing!

258
12:33.600 --> 12:35.550
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

259
12:35.870 --> 12:37.670
♪ We welcome workers and peasants from everywhere ♪

260
12:37.910 --> 12:39.670
♪ Officers and soldiers stand as equals ♪

261
12:40.080 --> 12:41.670
♪ No one oppresses another ♪

262
12:42.080 --> 12:43.750
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

263
12:44.030 --> 12:45.630
♪ Workers and peasants unite to fight the enemy ♪

264
12:45.840 --> 12:46.750
Look at that officer over there.

265
12:46.750 --> 12:48.790
Isn't he the one who smashed up our shop?

266
12:48.790 --> 12:50.240
That's him.

267
12:50.240 --> 12:51.440
Scoundrel!

268
12:52.720 --> 12:53.840
Stop hitting him!

269
12:54.630 --> 12:56.790
Ma'am, you can't do that! We have rules!

270
12:56.790 --> 12:57.450
Scoundrel!

271
12:57.550 --> 12:58.910
All right, that's enough!

272
12:58.910 --> 12:59.790
You really must stop!

273
12:59.790 --> 13:01.360
You really must stop, folks!

274
13:01.360 --> 13:02.550
Calm down, listen to me!

275
13:02.550 --> 13:04.000
We have strict rules. You can't hit him.

276
13:04.000 --> 13:08.720
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

277
13:10.070 --> 13:15.470
♪ We welcome workers and peasants from everywhere ♪

278
13:16.030 --> 13:17.840
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

279
13:18.670 --> 13:23.620
♪ Officers and soldiers stand as equals ♪

280
13:24.440 --> 13:29.240
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

281
13:29.390 --> 13:34.150
♪ After retirement, a soldier never worries about making a living ♪

282
13:35.670 --> 13:40.480
♪ Those who can work will find a job ♪

283
13:43.320 --> 13:45.170
Xie! It's Xie!

284
13:47.220 --> 13:47.650
It really is him!

285
13:47.650 --> 13:48.180
Xie!

286
13:50.610 --> 13:51.810
Xie, it really is you!

287
13:52.120 --> 13:52.750
Captain.

288
13:54.270 --> 13:58.660
Xie Xingguo, member of the 1st Army Corps' Publicity Department,

289
13:59.600 --> 14:01.320
reporting back for duty!

290
14:01.620 --> 14:02.820
Comrade Xie Xingguo,

291
14:03.180 --> 14:04.410
welcome back!

292
14:04.550 --> 14:05.630
Xie!

293
14:06.630 --> 14:07.270
Director Zhu.

294
14:07.270 --> 14:09.570
I finally found you.

295
14:09.630 --> 14:11.390
Come on, let's talk over there.

296
14:11.670 --> 14:12.400
It's good to have you back.

297
14:12.400 --> 14:13.280
Go on.

298
14:14.080 --> 14:15.240
Come on, everyone!

299
14:15.260 --> 14:16.530
Let's keep singing!

300
14:16.600 --> 14:17.170
Okay.

301
14:17.290 --> 14:19.050
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

302
14:19.390 --> 14:20.510
♪ We welcome workers and peasants from everywhere ♪

303
14:20.510 --> 14:22.510
Where did you catch up with the unit?

304
14:23.370 --> 14:27.400
I... I caught up with the unit by the Xiang River.

305
14:28.400 --> 14:29.730
I've been asking around

306
14:29.790 --> 14:32.320
about the Red Army's situation as I traveled.

307
14:32.530 --> 14:35.930
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

308
14:36.190 --> 14:38.050
When I crossed the Wujiang River,

309
14:38.520 --> 14:40.370
the ferryman told me

310
14:40.510 --> 14:42.570
that the Red Army had captured Zunyi.

311
14:43.400 --> 14:44.640
So I came to Zunyi,

312
14:45.630 --> 14:48.150
but... but you already left.

313
14:48.930 --> 14:51.050
I... I thought I'd never

314
14:51.960 --> 14:53.630
catch up with you again.

315
14:54.720 --> 14:57.550
Last night, I heard gunfire outside the city.

316
14:59.210 --> 15:01.570
They said the Red Army had returned.

317
15:03.400 --> 15:04.440
Don't cry.

318
15:04.490 --> 15:06.820
You're back with the unit now, aren't you?

319
15:08.720 --> 15:09.760
Director Zhu.

320
15:11.690 --> 15:15.970
I have important information to report to the organization.

321
15:16.220 --> 15:17.170
What is it?

322
15:27.070 --> 15:34.190
I, Xie Xingguo, messenger of the Red Army of the Xiang River Independent Company,

323
15:35.500 --> 15:37.360
reporting back for duty on behalf

324
15:38.400 --> 15:40.130
of all comrades in the company!

325
15:41.070 --> 15:43.000
Xiang River Independent Company?

326
15:43.430 --> 15:44.060
Yes.

327
15:45.560 --> 15:47.270
The Xiang River Independent Company

328
15:47.270 --> 15:49.470
was established in December last year,

329
15:50.090 --> 15:52.020
on the east bank of the Xiang River.

330
15:52.750 --> 15:55.270
Company Commander Peng Guangwen,

331
15:56.150 --> 15:57.480
Instructor Cai Zhong,

332
15:57.960 --> 16:00.320
Clerk Ma Yifeng,

333
16:01.020 --> 16:05.870
along with soldiers Chen Bolin, Zhang Ping...

334
16:07.520 --> 16:09.050
They...

335
16:09.580 --> 16:11.460
They never made it out.

336
16:12.410 --> 16:14.860
They never made it out.

337
16:19.220 --> 16:22.010
They never made it out.

338
16:24.300 --> 16:24.970
They...

339
16:25.840 --> 16:26.670
They...

340
16:28.270 --> 16:29.150
Kid.

341
16:30.800 --> 16:32.040
You are home.

342
16:34.900 --> 16:35.830
You are home now.

343
16:40.900 --> 16:44.620
Just now, the 1st Corps reported to the General Political Department,

344
16:44.620 --> 16:45.810
wanting to hold

345
16:46.260 --> 16:48.690
a meeting for Party activists

346
16:48.800 --> 16:51.130
with officers of company level and above.

347
16:51.390 --> 16:55.750
They also want to invite leaders of the Central Committee

348
16:56.130 --> 16:58.060
and the Military Commission to attend and deliver speeches.

349
16:58.060 --> 16:59.010
I think

350
16:59.370 --> 17:01.090
we can use this opportunity

351
17:01.720 --> 17:04.109
to further explain the significance of the Zunyi Conference resolution

352
17:04.109 --> 17:06.200
once again, in greater detail.

353
17:07.050 --> 17:09.050
Then let's have Mao prepare a report

354
17:09.319 --> 17:10.349
and let him deliver the main report.

355
17:10.349 --> 17:11.000
Okay.

356
17:11.970 --> 17:13.569
Well, it's like we're people

357
17:13.640 --> 17:16.089
who returned to a place we once abandoned.

358
17:17.230 --> 17:18.560
It's been over a month,

359
17:19.020 --> 17:20.359
but it feels like yesterday.

360
17:20.359 --> 17:22.349
Back then, we left Zunyi in a hurry,

361
17:22.490 --> 17:24.119
and were forced to cross the Chishui River to the west.

362
17:24.119 --> 17:27.680
Now we've crossed back east and retaken Zunyi.

363
17:28.300 --> 17:30.500
The situation has changed completely.

364
17:32.840 --> 17:34.240
Where's Comrade Zedong?

365
17:34.680 --> 17:37.190
He went to the field hospital to visit the wounded.

366
17:37.190 --> 17:38.200
Slow down, Jiaxiang.

367
17:38.200 --> 17:39.400
Here, let me help you.

368
17:40.030 --> 17:40.640
Careful.

369
17:46.740 --> 17:47.700
Slow down.

370
17:47.960 --> 17:49.360
How old are you, young man?

371
17:49.360 --> 17:50.040
I'm 15.

372
17:51.260 --> 17:53.010
Did you run into any danger on the way?

373
17:53.010 --> 17:53.680
No.

374
17:54.140 --> 17:54.930
We're here.

375
17:58.570 --> 18:00.100
Political Commissar Yang.

376
18:01.880 --> 18:02.800
What's going on?

377
18:02.800 --> 18:03.690
This young man says

378
18:03.690 --> 18:05.020
he wants to return something to the Red Army hospital.

379
18:05.020 --> 18:06.220
I'm taking him there.

380
18:08.170 --> 18:09.060
Return what?

381
18:26.010 --> 18:27.300
Long Yuqin?

382
18:27.410 --> 18:29.430
He was a doctor in our Red Army hospital.

383
18:29.430 --> 18:31.830
When the troops first withdrew from Zunyi,

384
18:32.020 --> 18:33.770
he stayed behind to treat the locals

385
18:33.770 --> 18:35.030
and missed his chance to rejoin the unit.

386
18:35.030 --> 18:36.430
The local militia caught him

387
18:36.430 --> 18:37.430
and beat him to death.

388
18:37.430 --> 18:38.790
He didn't have to die.

389
18:40.660 --> 18:43.460
He died trying to save my father and the villagers.

390
18:44.050 --> 18:46.580
We all called him the "Red Army Bodhisattva."

391
18:46.600 --> 18:47.520
Before he died,

392
18:48.210 --> 18:49.590
he asked me to return this medicine chest

393
18:49.590 --> 18:51.140
to the Red Army hospital.

394
18:51.530 --> 18:53.590
I've been looking for you for so long.

395
18:56.350 --> 18:57.160
Thank you,

396
18:57.880 --> 18:58.830
young man.

397
18:59.930 --> 19:03.530
After you return the medicine chest, you should head home early.

398
19:03.700 --> 19:04.660
Take him to get something to eat.

399
19:04.660 --> 19:05.270
Yes, sir.

400
19:05.760 --> 19:06.960
Follow me, young man.

401
19:07.000 --> 19:07.530
Come on.

402
19:07.650 --> 19:08.890
Comrade.

403
19:10.160 --> 19:11.420
Are you in charge here?

404
19:13.160 --> 19:14.490
Is there anything else?

405
19:14.740 --> 19:15.660
Please take me in!

406
19:15.660 --> 19:16.050
Come on, get up.

407
19:16.050 --> 19:16.920
I'm not leaving.

408
19:16.920 --> 19:17.980
What are you doing?

409
19:19.880 --> 19:20.970
The "Red Army Bodhisattva" promised me

410
19:20.970 --> 19:22.900
that he'd help me join the Red Army.

411
19:27.540 --> 19:28.400
How old are you?

412
19:28.640 --> 19:29.480
I'm 15.

413
19:30.140 --> 19:31.640
Why do you want to join the Red Army?

414
19:31.640 --> 19:33.310
The "Red Army Bodhisattva" said

415
19:33.310 --> 19:34.530
all poor people should join the Red Army.

416
19:34.530 --> 19:37.930
That way those KMT bastards won't be able to run wild anymore.

417
19:38.240 --> 19:40.040
He promised he'd help me enlist.

418
19:42.470 --> 19:44.200
Please let me join the Red Army.

419
19:44.640 --> 19:45.790
I can endure hardship.

420
19:45.790 --> 19:46.590
I'm strong.

421
19:47.270 --> 19:47.990
I run fast.

422
19:48.310 --> 19:49.460
I can climb mountains.

423
19:49.460 --> 19:50.890
I can climb trees, too. Look if you don't believe it!

424
19:50.890 --> 19:51.550
Be careful.

425
20:00.890 --> 20:01.960
What's your name?

426
20:02.260 --> 20:03.470
My name is Yun Guichuan.

427
20:03.470 --> 20:04.520
Yunguichuan.

428
20:05.350 --> 20:06.170
That's a good name.

429
20:06.170 --> 20:08.060
The "Red Army Bodhisattva" gave me that name

430
20:08.060 --> 20:10.120
He said it's the grandest name of all.

431
20:10.190 --> 20:10.950
Comrade,

432
20:11.430 --> 20:12.890
will you let me join or not?

433
20:14.760 --> 20:15.320
Not bad.

434
20:15.890 --> 20:17.090
Do you think he'll do?

435
20:17.240 --> 20:18.590
Yes, absolutely.

436
20:18.830 --> 20:20.510
With his agility,

437
20:20.890 --> 20:22.110
he'll be useful in our Regiment.

438
20:22.110 --> 20:23.170
Come down quickly.

439
20:28.010 --> 20:29.530
All right, Yun Guichuan.

440
20:30.250 --> 20:32.860
From now on, you're a soldier in the 4th Red Regiment.

441
20:32.860 --> 20:33.580
Yes, sir!

442
20:35.050 --> 20:36.710
Use your right hand to salute.

443
20:37.560 --> 20:38.190
Like this.

444
20:38.650 --> 20:39.360
Yes, sir!

445
20:43.580 --> 20:44.180
All right.

446
20:44.380 --> 20:45.970
First, I'll take you to return the medicine chest,

447
20:45.970 --> 20:46.870
then we'll get you registered.

448
20:46.870 --> 20:47.700
Let's go.

449
20:48.420 --> 20:49.340
He's pretty nimble.

450
20:49.340 --> 20:50.340
He climbed right up the pole.

451
20:50.340 --> 20:51.800
That gave me quite a scare!

452
20:53.940 --> 20:55.530
Long Yuqin,

453
20:55.940 --> 20:58.510
based on the historical figure Long Siquan,

454
20:58.580 --> 20:59.620
was from Guangxi.

455
21:00.080 --> 21:01.880
In January 1935,

456
21:02.180 --> 21:05.780
he stayed behind to treat local people, failed to rejoin his unit

457
21:05.850 --> 21:08.050
and was brutally murdered by the enemy.

458
21:09.180 --> 21:11.370
The local people were grateful for his kindness,

459
21:11.370 --> 21:13.630
calling him the "Red Army Bodhisattva."

460
21:14.050 --> 21:15.730
They buried him where he was killed,

461
21:15.730 --> 21:17.590
named his grave the Red Army Tomb,

462
21:18.450 --> 21:20.980
and returned each year to pay their respects.

463
21:21.110 --> 21:22.710
In March 1954,

464
21:23.250 --> 21:25.580
the Zunyi Municipal Government moved the Red Army Tomb

465
21:25.580 --> 21:28.260
to the Zunyi Red Army Martyrs Cemetery.

466
21:31.770 --> 21:39.760
[Red Army Field Hospital, Zunyi, Guizhou]

467
21:35.970 --> 21:37.380
Bring me some more gauze.

468
21:37.900 --> 21:38.340
Okay.

469
21:39.490 --> 21:40.490
Corps Commander.

470
21:40.820 --> 21:41.820
Corps Commander.

471
21:43.670 --> 21:44.660
Corps Commander.

472
21:44.660 --> 21:45.610
Corps Commander.

473
21:45.610 --> 21:46.610
Corps Commander.

474
21:46.690 --> 21:47.690
Corps Commander.

475
22:24.770 --> 22:25.810
Corps Commander Peng.

476
22:25.810 --> 22:26.810
Corps Commander.

477
22:33.680 --> 22:34.390
Doctor.

478
22:36.210 --> 22:37.340
Can you save his life

479
22:38.900 --> 22:40.050
this time?

480
22:41.210 --> 22:42.140
It's hard to say.

481
22:42.620 --> 22:45.480
This time, we'll have to amputate the leg at the hip.

482
22:45.860 --> 22:46.950
We're out of medicine

483
22:46.950 --> 22:48.750
and the weather is cold and damp.

484
22:49.100 --> 22:51.100
If the wound gets infected again...

485
23:13.290 --> 23:14.290
Corps Commander,

486
23:14.490 --> 23:15.750
why are you here again?

487
23:16.010 --> 23:16.860
Young lad,

488
23:17.400 --> 23:19.210
you've had three amputations in half a month.

489
23:19.210 --> 23:20.740
I was here for the first two.

490
23:20.770 --> 23:23.360
How could I possibly miss this one?

491
23:23.380 --> 23:25.350
[Zhong Chibing, Political Commissar of the 12th Regiment of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

492
23:26.580 --> 23:27.310
Does it hurt?

493
23:27.690 --> 23:28.620
Yell if it hurts.

494
23:29.290 --> 23:30.130
It doesn't hurt.

495
23:30.130 --> 23:30.930
Liar!

496
23:31.820 --> 23:32.450
Kid.

497
23:32.770 --> 23:35.730
Why are you acting tough in front of me?

498
23:37.300 --> 23:39.130
This time at Loushanguan,

499
23:39.660 --> 23:41.290
you showed what the Red Army is made of.

500
23:41.290 --> 23:42.220
Yell if it hurts!

501
23:42.690 --> 23:43.950
Even if you have to cry,

502
23:44.010 --> 23:45.270
there's no shame in it.

503
23:45.730 --> 23:46.730
Corps Commander,

504
23:47.620 --> 23:50.180
give me a straight answer this time.

505
23:50.950 --> 23:54.000
Can I still stay with the army?

506
24:07.290 --> 24:08.820
I lost my legs,

507
24:08.900 --> 24:10.900
but I can still use my hands to shoot.

508
24:11.180 --> 24:12.690
And I'm smart.

509
24:12.690 --> 24:14.340
I can command troops in battle.

510
24:14.340 --> 24:15.290
I also have...

511
24:19.100 --> 24:20.830
Corps Commander, I'm not afraid of pain.

512
24:20.830 --> 24:24.230
I'm not afraid of having my legs sawed off. I'm just afraid...

513
24:25.800 --> 24:28.430
the Red Army won't want me anymore.

514
24:33.690 --> 24:34.550
Zhong Chibing,

515
24:35.040 --> 24:36.000
listen to me.

516
24:37.380 --> 24:40.450
I, Peng Dehuai, give you my word right now.

517
24:40.750 --> 24:41.950
As long as you hold on,

518
24:42.730 --> 24:44.660
as long as you're still breathing,

519
24:44.900 --> 24:46.860
we will never leave you behind!

520
25:01.290 --> 25:02.580
Corps Commander,

521
25:02.940 --> 25:05.030
it hurts!

522
25:05.050 --> 25:07.120
If it hurts, yell it out.

523
25:09.220 --> 25:11.140
You'll feel better once you let it out.

524
25:11.140 --> 25:12.890
It hurts!

525
25:13.580 --> 25:15.510
Let it out. You'll feel better.

526
25:34.530 --> 25:35.860
Company Commander Mao.

527
25:35.940 --> 25:36.530
Company Commander Mao is here.

528
25:36.530 --> 25:38.260
Hello, Company Commander Mao.

529
25:46.110 --> 25:47.040
Reporting, sir!

530
25:48.240 --> 25:48.800
Come in.

531
25:51.690 --> 25:52.890
Regiment Commander.

532
25:58.010 --> 25:58.660
Well,

533
26:00.410 --> 26:01.470
take a look at this.

534
26:02.050 --> 26:04.690
This is the receipt the Reception Station gave me.

535
26:04.690 --> 26:06.450
No prisoner in our regiment

536
26:06.450 --> 26:07.910
outranks this one, right?

537
26:08.100 --> 26:09.100
Of course not.

538
26:10.320 --> 26:11.010
Good.

539
26:13.010 --> 26:15.420
Then this gun...

540
26:15.450 --> 26:16.500
Zhenhua.

541
26:17.880 --> 26:20.480
I need to point out a few problems with this gun.

542
26:20.730 --> 26:22.130
Well, every gun has its flaws.

543
26:22.130 --> 26:22.730
It has strong firepower.

544
26:22.730 --> 26:24.420
No, no. This gun has a lot of problems.

545
26:24.420 --> 26:24.990
You don't know much about this one.

546
26:24.990 --> 26:26.230
Let me explain them to you one by one.

547
26:26.230 --> 26:27.420
Let go. Let go.

548
26:29.010 --> 26:30.900
First of all,

549
26:31.530 --> 26:32.730
this gun is too heavy.

550
26:33.040 --> 26:34.760
It's over 1.5 kilos.

551
26:35.140 --> 26:36.300
You see, I'm a big guy,

552
26:36.300 --> 26:38.360
but carrying it around while running

553
26:40.940 --> 26:42.210
is a real pain in the butt.

554
26:42.210 --> 26:43.810
After a forced march,

555
26:43.840 --> 26:45.170
my leg were all bruised.

556
26:46.030 --> 26:47.630
Zhenhua, your company

557
26:47.900 --> 26:49.700
is the vanguard of our regiment.

558
26:49.900 --> 26:52.210
After a forced march,

559
26:52.610 --> 26:53.400
can your legs

560
26:53.420 --> 26:55.220
really take that kind of strain?

561
26:55.310 --> 26:56.420
All guns are heavy.

562
26:56.770 --> 26:57.820
What matters is that it's got strong firepower.

563
26:57.820 --> 26:59.900
Hey, I know it.

564
26:59.900 --> 27:01.810
But you have to know how old this gun is.

565
27:01.810 --> 27:02.420
Got it?

566
27:02.820 --> 27:05.960
This revolver was

567
27:05.980 --> 27:08.790
manufactured in Germany in 1879.

568
27:09.380 --> 27:12.420
That was the fifth year of the Guangxu Emperor's reign.

569
27:12.420 --> 27:13.820
Or the sixth year, maybe.

570
27:13.820 --> 27:14.970
How old are you?

571
27:15.620 --> 27:16.620
I was born in 1910.

572
27:17.860 --> 27:18.660
See?

573
27:19.250 --> 27:20.800
This gun is older than your father

574
27:20.800 --> 27:22.620
and almost as old as your grandfather.

575
27:22.620 --> 27:23.480
It's an old gun.

576
27:23.670 --> 27:25.800
You're taking an old grandpa into battle.

577
27:25.800 --> 27:27.160
What if it jams?

578
27:27.190 --> 27:28.650
What will you do then? Right?

579
27:28.650 --> 27:29.120
Right.

580
27:32.690 --> 27:35.490
The thing is it has strong firepower.

581
27:35.550 --> 27:36.510
I know it has strong firepower.

582
27:36.510 --> 27:37.840
I never said it doesn't.

583
27:37.870 --> 27:40.330
But you have to be able to get it to fire first.

584
27:40.940 --> 27:43.140
This gun has a major flaw.

585
27:43.510 --> 27:45.240
It doesn't have an ejector rod.

586
27:45.530 --> 27:46.770
Every time you finish shooting,

587
27:46.770 --> 27:48.420
you have to use this cleaning rod

588
27:48.420 --> 27:49.690
to push out

589
27:49.720 --> 27:51.200
the spent cartridges one by one.

590
27:51.200 --> 27:53.250
On a battlefield, things change in an instant.

591
27:53.250 --> 27:54.050
It's a hassle!

592
27:54.900 --> 27:56.360
So after thinking it over,

593
27:56.760 --> 27:57.470
Zhenhua,

594
27:58.900 --> 28:00.250
I think

595
28:00.250 --> 28:03.110
this Mauser pistol suits you better.

596
28:03.140 --> 28:04.380
Here, take it.

597
28:07.070 --> 28:07.820
This one's more suitable.

598
28:07.820 --> 28:10.150
Regiment Commander, you can drop the act.

599
28:10.490 --> 28:12.250
You don't want to give me the revolver, do you?

600
28:12.250 --> 28:14.580
The Chief of Staff's standing at attention

601
28:14.580 --> 28:15.490
at the Reception Station.

602
28:15.490 --> 28:16.560
If you don't believe me, come with me.

603
28:16.560 --> 28:17.740
I'll take you to see him now.

604
28:17.740 --> 28:18.340
No need.

605
28:18.340 --> 28:19.690
Do you think I don't trust you?

606
28:19.690 --> 28:21.820
Do I really need to go and see for myself?

607
28:21.820 --> 28:23.180
A promise is a promise.

608
28:23.210 --> 28:24.810
How could I go back on my word?

609
28:30.770 --> 28:31.290
Take it.

610
28:31.420 --> 28:32.090
Great!

611
28:39.890 --> 28:41.090
The ammo is precious.

612
28:41.550 --> 28:43.010
It's 10.6 millimeters in caliber.

613
28:43.010 --> 28:44.220
And we have no way to loot any more.

614
28:44.220 --> 28:45.600
Every shot counts.

615
28:46.530 --> 28:49.190
Let's see what you'll do when you run out of ammo.

616
28:49.950 --> 28:50.590
Okay.

617
28:54.950 --> 28:55.870
Well,

618
28:58.020 --> 28:59.420
the hammer is a bit stiff,

619
29:00.590 --> 29:02.660
and the safety is on the left.

620
29:03.580 --> 29:05.540
You'll need to use some force when you cock it.

621
29:05.540 --> 29:06.450
I know, Regiment Commander.

622
29:06.450 --> 29:07.060
Now that you've given it to me,

623
29:07.060 --> 29:08.920
I'll figure out how to use it myself.

624
29:08.920 --> 29:10.720
Thank you, Regiment Commander.

625
29:12.430 --> 29:14.040
Company Commander Mao,

626
29:15.660 --> 29:16.420
this gun is awesome!

627
29:16.420 --> 29:16.770
Not bad, huh?

628
29:16.770 --> 29:18.450
Impressive, Company Commander Mao!

629
29:18.450 --> 29:19.910
Oh, it's nothing special.

630
29:20.030 --> 29:21.630
I'll let you try it sometime.

631
29:40.100 --> 29:40.730
Company Commander.

632
29:40.730 --> 29:42.450
You actually got the revolver?

633
29:42.450 --> 29:43.010
Company Commander,

634
29:43.010 --> 29:44.830
You actually got the Regiment Commander's gun?

635
29:44.830 --> 29:45.960
That's incredible!

636
29:46.040 --> 29:48.700
Company Commander Mao, now you've got two guns!

637
29:49.250 --> 29:50.190
Company Commander Mao.

638
29:50.190 --> 29:51.850
Did he really give you the gun?

639
29:52.870 --> 29:53.870
Of course he did!

640
29:55.500 --> 29:57.900
Doesn't it look like it was made just for me?

641
29:59.340 --> 30:01.400
It's like it was tailor-made for you!

642
30:07.340 --> 30:09.000
Not bad, Comrade Mao Zhenhua.

643
30:09.180 --> 30:10.380
You've even strapped on your gun,

644
30:10.380 --> 30:12.210
showing off and acting all high and mighty.

645
30:12.210 --> 30:13.470
Political Commissar,

646
30:13.660 --> 30:14.420
take a look.

647
30:18.020 --> 30:18.830
Political Commissar,

648
30:18.830 --> 30:20.890
that didn't sound like a compliment.

649
30:21.040 --> 30:23.520
I earned this fair and square.

650
30:24.050 --> 30:24.860
You really

651
30:24.890 --> 30:27.090
broke our Regiment Commander's heart.

652
30:30.850 --> 30:32.250
Don't... don't scare me.

653
30:32.410 --> 30:34.700
What did I do? How did I break his heart?

654
30:35.900 --> 30:37.830
Do you know the history of that gun?

655
30:37.980 --> 30:38.900
What is it?

656
30:39.580 --> 30:40.490
This gun

657
30:40.600 --> 30:42.280
was captured from Zhang Huizan

658
30:42.280 --> 30:44.100
during the first Counter-Encirclement Campaign.

659
30:44.100 --> 30:44.970
Commander-in-Chief Zhu

660
30:44.970 --> 30:47.100
kept it as his own sidearm at that time.

661
30:47.250 --> 30:49.290
Later, during the fourth Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

662
30:49.290 --> 30:51.010
our Regiment Commander distinguished himself in battle,

663
30:51.010 --> 30:52.660
and Commander-in-Chief Zhu personally

664
30:52.660 --> 30:54.010
presented the gun to him as a reward.

665
30:54.010 --> 30:56.270
So tell me, haven't you broken his heart?

666
30:59.870 --> 31:00.870
Believe it or not,

667
31:00.940 --> 31:04.200
the Regiment Commander is probably swinging an axe in his room right now.

668
31:04.200 --> 31:05.050
I...

669
31:19.220 --> 31:19.970
Get someone to help

670
31:19.970 --> 31:20.780
move these things inside.

671
31:20.780 --> 31:21.540
Sure thing.

672
31:21.790 --> 31:22.720
You come with me.

673
31:37.390 --> 31:38.720
Company Commander Mao.

674
31:38.780 --> 31:39.970
Why are you here again?

675
31:39.970 --> 31:40.900
Get back to work.

676
31:44.530 --> 31:45.080
Reporting!

677
31:45.080 --> 31:45.560
Come in.

678
31:47.200 --> 31:48.130
Why are you back?

679
31:48.570 --> 31:49.500
What do you want?

680
31:53.950 --> 31:55.610
I don't want this gun anymore.

681
32:00.770 --> 32:02.100
Hey, what are you doing?

682
32:03.240 --> 32:05.170
Haven't you always liked this gun?

683
32:05.420 --> 32:06.290
Besides,

684
32:06.450 --> 32:08.230
I can't go back on my word, right?

685
32:08.230 --> 32:09.140
Just take it.

686
32:11.040 --> 32:12.360
You'd better keep it.

687
32:13.250 --> 32:14.900
Next time, I'll capture someone like

688
32:14.900 --> 32:16.300
Wang Huizan or Li Huizan,

689
32:16.450 --> 32:19.380
and earn a gun of my own from the Commander-in-Chief.

690
32:28.030 --> 32:28.990
Well,

691
32:29.770 --> 32:31.630
did someone say something to you?

692
32:33.990 --> 32:34.750
No.

693
32:36.750 --> 32:40.680
I can't break your heart by keeping something that means so much to you.

694
32:44.140 --> 32:46.330
Mao Zhenhua, Mao Zhenhua.

695
32:46.660 --> 32:47.660
Didn't I tell you?

696
32:47.770 --> 32:50.060
The Mauser pistol suits you the best.

697
32:50.580 --> 32:51.730
Wasn't I right?

698
32:53.610 --> 32:54.940
It can fire single shots

699
32:55.150 --> 32:56.110
and fire in full-auto

700
32:56.110 --> 32:57.830
It's a fine weapon! Take it!

701
33:01.470 --> 33:02.530
After all this,

702
33:02.750 --> 33:04.610
this Mauser pistol is the best for me.

703
33:04.610 --> 33:06.800
The thing is that it feels right in your hands.

704
33:06.800 --> 33:07.630
Yeah.

705
33:07.920 --> 33:09.210
All right, Mao Zhenhua.

706
33:09.210 --> 33:10.940
You don't have to feel wronged.

707
33:11.140 --> 33:12.010
I'll give you someone

708
33:12.010 --> 33:13.770
that's better than this Mauser pistol.

709
33:13.770 --> 33:14.480
Yun Guichuan.

710
33:14.480 --> 33:15.240
Coming!

711
33:15.800 --> 33:16.390
Here!

712
33:17.050 --> 33:18.710
Take a look. What do you think?

713
33:21.650 --> 33:24.120
Political Commissar, he's just a kid.

714
33:24.280 --> 33:25.620
Does he even know how to use a gun?

715
33:25.620 --> 33:27.920
And how could he be better than a Mauser pistol?

716
33:27.920 --> 33:29.380
What? You look down on him?

717
33:29.450 --> 33:30.640
His name is Yun Guichuan.

718
33:30.640 --> 33:31.900
He's remarkably agile

719
33:32.290 --> 33:33.900
and has great potential.

720
33:33.930 --> 33:35.660
I'll leave him to your Company.

721
33:35.690 --> 33:36.550
Train him well.

722
33:36.730 --> 33:37.860
Political Commissar.

723
33:37.860 --> 33:39.060
Regiment Commander.

724
33:39.210 --> 33:41.210
We guarantee we'll get the job done!

725
33:45.840 --> 33:47.640
I think the kid will do just fine.

726
33:48.400 --> 33:49.000
Yun Guichuan!

727
33:49.000 --> 33:49.480
Here!

728
33:49.560 --> 33:51.420
I'll take you to get your uniform.

729
33:52.150 --> 33:52.800
Okay.

730
33:55.100 --> 33:55.940
How old are you?

731
33:55.940 --> 33:56.660
I'm 15.

732
34:04.760 --> 34:05.560
Thanks.

733
34:07.490 --> 34:09.489
You don't have to swing that axe now.

734
34:13.630 --> 34:15.100
Look how things worked out.

735
34:15.100 --> 34:18.030
After all that fuss, the gun's back where it belongs!

736
34:20.739 --> 34:22.540
First, let's get you cleaned up.

737
34:23.570 --> 34:25.179
Take a nice bath first.

738
34:29.330 --> 34:31.730
Let's get you cleaned up and looking sharp.

739
34:38.750 --> 34:39.350
Come on.

740
34:39.940 --> 34:41.469
Leaders, the meal is ready.

741
34:41.780 --> 34:42.380
Good.

742
34:43.239 --> 34:45.900
Let's wait for Comrade Zedong and eat together.

743
34:46.010 --> 34:46.650
Okay.

744
34:49.659 --> 34:50.449
Hu.

745
34:51.219 --> 34:52.420
Is the Chairman back?

746
34:52.489 --> 34:53.380
Is Mao back?

747
34:54.989 --> 34:55.840
He's back.

748
35:05.380 --> 35:06.380
Comrade Zedong.

749
35:18.490 --> 35:19.450
What a feast.

750
35:20.840 --> 35:23.320
These were captured by various units

751
35:23.450 --> 35:24.900
and sent to the Military Commission by the cartload.

752
35:24.900 --> 35:25.480
So we decided to

753
35:25.480 --> 35:27.410
give everyone a better meal today.

754
35:27.520 --> 35:28.080
Good.

755
35:28.420 --> 35:29.750
We fought a good battle,

756
35:29.780 --> 35:30.830
and there's plenty to eat.

757
35:30.830 --> 35:31.410
Let's eat.

758
35:31.410 --> 35:31.890
Good.

759
35:42.340 --> 35:43.010
Here.

760
35:45.950 --> 35:46.590
Commander-in-Chief Zhu.

761
35:46.590 --> 35:47.230
Thanks.

762
35:53.800 --> 35:54.680
Reporting!

763
35:56.130 --> 35:57.020
Vice Chairman Zhou,

764
35:57.020 --> 35:59.950
The Second Bureau has just cracked a coded telegram.

765
36:02.970 --> 36:04.970
Chiang Kai-shek has arrived in Chongqing

766
36:04.970 --> 36:05.900
to personally direct

767
36:05.900 --> 36:08.360
the next encirclement campaign against us.

768
36:09.300 --> 36:11.650
Chiang Kai-shek just won't let us enjoy a meal.

769
36:11.650 --> 36:13.090
What does the telegram say?

770
36:13.090 --> 36:15.780
He ordered the Hunan Army, Guizhou Army, and Central Army

771
36:15.780 --> 36:17.510
to blockade the Wujiang River;

772
36:17.650 --> 36:19.490
ordered the Sichuan Army and Guizhou Army

773
36:19.490 --> 36:21.530
to attack Loushanguan and Zunyi;

774
36:21.560 --> 36:22.650
ordered Zhou Hunyuan's troops

775
36:22.650 --> 36:24.740
to assemble from the south towards Yaxi,

776
36:24.740 --> 36:27.570
and attack Zunyi from the southwest.

777
36:27.780 --> 36:31.910
Sichuan Army, Hunan Army, Guizhou Army, Yunnan Army, and the Central Army

778
36:32.370 --> 36:33.730
have all been mobilized.

779
36:33.730 --> 36:35.990
That's quite a force they've assembled.

780
36:36.180 --> 36:38.110
They're casting another wide net.

781
36:38.130 --> 36:40.060
It seems Chiang has lost his patience,

782
36:40.060 --> 36:41.570
and has decided to take personal command.

783
36:41.570 --> 36:43.370
He's coming at us aggressively.

784
36:43.860 --> 36:45.920
Every time a major battle approaches,

785
36:45.920 --> 36:47.980
Chiang always takes direct control.

786
36:49.340 --> 36:50.270
Comrade Zedong,

787
36:50.310 --> 36:52.340
how should we respond?

788
36:53.240 --> 36:55.440
We'll deal with whatever comes our way.

789
36:56.610 --> 37:00.010
We'll concentrate our forces and take a bite out of the enemy,

790
37:00.940 --> 37:02.220
turning the tables and seizing the initiative.

791
37:02.220 --> 37:05.140
Then which enemy force should we target?

792
37:06.530 --> 37:08.260
If we want to gnaw on a bone, we should gnaw on a hard one.

793
37:08.260 --> 37:10.790
Of course, we should attack the Central Army.

794
37:11.000 --> 37:13.860
Zhou Hunyuan has chased us all the way from Jiangxi.

795
37:14.050 --> 37:15.580
Now he's on... the east bank

796
37:15.700 --> 37:18.490
of the Chishui River, holding a military parade.

797
37:18.490 --> 37:20.220
The military parade has been going on for over 10 days.

798
37:20.220 --> 37:21.260
They must be very tired.

799
37:21.260 --> 37:23.570
When the enemy is tired, we strike!

800
37:24.050 --> 37:25.570
We can't miss this opportunity.

801
37:25.570 --> 37:26.890
To destroy Zhou Hunyuan's forces,

802
37:26.890 --> 37:28.660
we must plan carefully

803
37:29.090 --> 37:31.170
to make sure we have the upper hand.

804
37:31.420 --> 37:32.870
First, the 9th Army Corps

805
37:33.570 --> 37:36.940
will continue feigning attacks around the Tongzi and Zunyi,

806
37:36.940 --> 37:38.940
to prevent the Sichuan Army from moving east.

807
37:38.940 --> 37:40.300
The main forces of the 1st, 3rd, and 5th Army Corps,

808
37:40.300 --> 37:42.260
and the main force of the Cadre Regiment will advance west,

809
37:42.260 --> 37:44.130
set up an encirclement near Yaxi

810
37:44.380 --> 37:45.530
to ambush Zhou Hunyuan's troops.

811
37:45.530 --> 37:47.330
We'll set as many traps as we can.

812
37:47.420 --> 37:48.770
Then we'll wipe them out in a single blow!

813
37:48.770 --> 37:49.750
According to our intelligence,

814
37:49.750 --> 37:51.860
Zhou Hunyuan's troops move very quickly.

815
37:51.860 --> 37:53.300
Since we are setting up a tactical pocket,

816
37:53.300 --> 37:55.380
we must get ahead of the enemy.

817
37:55.970 --> 37:57.480
Since Chiang Kai-shek is centralizing power,

818
37:57.480 --> 37:58.820
then we'll do the opposite.

819
37:58.820 --> 38:00.480
Now, the situation is urgent.

820
38:00.610 --> 38:03.380
I propose we convene a Politburo meeting immediately

821
38:03.380 --> 38:05.090
to decide whether to establish

822
38:05.090 --> 38:07.220
a special forward command headquarters.

823
38:07.220 --> 38:09.350
Comrade Zhu De will serve as Commander

824
38:09.570 --> 38:11.970
and Comrade Mao Zedong as Political Commissar

825
38:11.970 --> 38:14.650
with direct command of this campaign.

826
38:15.120 --> 38:16.680
What do you think?

827
38:19.860 --> 38:20.790
Comrade Zedong,

828
38:20.960 --> 38:23.400
you mustn't turn it down this time.

829
38:25.420 --> 38:26.260
Old fella,

830
38:26.610 --> 38:28.450
it's been over two years,

831
38:28.780 --> 38:30.840
Zhu and Mao are working together again.

832
38:30.840 --> 38:33.100
Are you still going to decline this time?

833
38:39.420 --> 38:40.270
No.

834
38:52.650 --> 38:57.600
[The southern mountain region of Zunyi, Guizhou]

835
39:17.710 --> 39:18.420
Reporting!

836
39:18.990 --> 39:21.320
Urgent telegram from the Generalissimo!

837
39:29.070 --> 39:31.820
[Zhou Hunyuan, Commander of the 2nd Column, 2nd Route Army of the "Pursuit and Suppression" Forces, KMT Army]

838
39:30.610 --> 39:31.700
A new order?

839
39:32.810 --> 39:34.470
He's urging us to move faster.

840
39:36.570 --> 39:39.010
This order bypassed Commander-in-Chief Xue

841
39:39.010 --> 39:40.340
and came directly to us.

842
39:40.610 --> 39:41.530
Now even Commander-in-Chief Xue

843
39:41.530 --> 39:43.130
has become his messenger.

844
39:44.380 --> 39:45.300
Order all divisions

845
39:45.300 --> 39:46.260
to carry out the order.

846
39:46.260 --> 39:47.660
Move as fast as possible!

847
39:47.780 --> 39:48.430
Yes, sir!

848
39:48.940 --> 39:49.610
Speed up.

849
39:49.670 --> 39:50.760
All troops, move faster!

850
39:50.760 --> 39:51.470
Hurry!

851
39:56.800 --> 40:01.860
[Fan Shaozeng's Residence, Chongqing]

852
40:08.130 --> 40:09.340
What's the situation?

853
40:09.340 --> 40:10.130
Go ahead.

854
40:10.340 --> 40:11.340
Report, Generalissimo.

855
40:11.340 --> 40:12.380
This is the Zunyi reconnaissance report

856
40:12.380 --> 40:13.440
from the Air Force.

857
40:13.780 --> 40:15.470
Around 3 PM today,

858
40:15.820 --> 40:17.050
more than 10,000 Communist soldiers

859
40:17.050 --> 40:19.230
were moving southwest toward Yaxikou.

860
40:19.230 --> 40:20.310
Yaxikou?

861
40:23.610 --> 40:26.090
Heading toward Yaxikou...

862
40:38.240 --> 40:40.300
What if the Communist Army isn't making a feint?

863
40:40.300 --> 40:42.300
What if they're planning an ambush?

864
40:44.170 --> 40:46.420
The devil is in the details when it comes to planning.

865
40:46.420 --> 40:47.650
We must never forget

866
40:48.610 --> 40:50.290
that we're dealing with Mao Zedong.

867
40:50.290 --> 40:51.150
If that's the case,

868
40:51.150 --> 40:52.950
Zhou Hunyuan could be in danger.

869
40:52.970 --> 40:53.900
Generalissimo.

870
40:53.940 --> 40:54.490
By now,

871
40:54.530 --> 40:56.530
Zhou Hunyuan's troops should have passed Changgan Mountain.

872
40:56.530 --> 40:57.820
Send a telegram to Zhou Hunyuan.

873
40:57.820 --> 40:59.220
Tell him to stop his eastward advance

874
40:59.220 --> 41:00.450
and return to Changgan Mountain.

875
41:00.450 --> 41:01.520
They need to fortify positions there

876
41:01.520 --> 41:02.490
and get into defensive positions.

877
41:02.490 --> 41:03.700
Keep the Communist Army under observation.

878
41:03.700 --> 41:05.410
Also, send a telegram to Wu Qiwei:

879
41:05.410 --> 41:06.940
Stand by on the south bank of the Wujiang River.

880
41:06.940 --> 41:08.490
If the Communist Army moves west,

881
41:08.490 --> 41:09.450
pursue and attack them immediately.

882
41:09.450 --> 41:10.650
Yes, Generalissimo!

883
41:24.820 --> 41:25.530
By the way,

884
41:25.780 --> 41:28.130
stop using the old cipher.

885
41:28.340 --> 41:29.230
Tell the cipher office

886
41:29.230 --> 41:30.450
to issue a new codebook.

887
41:30.450 --> 41:31.650
Yes, Generalissimo!

888
42:15.870 --> 42:16.580
Reporting!

889
42:16.900 --> 42:19.960
ommander, an urgent telegram from the Generalissimo.

890
42:28.170 --> 42:29.050
Commander,

891
42:29.180 --> 42:30.090
what happened?

892
42:30.530 --> 42:32.190
The Generalissimo ordered us

893
42:32.220 --> 42:34.280
to stop advancing east immediately,

894
42:34.700 --> 42:36.340
retreat to the Changgan Mountain line,

895
42:36.340 --> 42:38.470
and build fortifications on the spot.

896
42:39.010 --> 42:41.200
Didn't he order us to march day and night earlier today

897
42:41.200 --> 42:42.130
to attack Zunyi?

898
42:42.490 --> 42:44.580
Why did he change his mind so suddenly?

899
42:44.580 --> 42:46.740
It's not the first time he has done this.

900
42:46.740 --> 42:49.340
Should we ask Commander Xue for instructions?

901
42:49.910 --> 42:50.970
Is that necessary?

902
42:52.010 --> 42:52.900
Pass on my order.

903
42:52.900 --> 42:55.100
The rear guard takes the lead. Retreat.

904
42:56.050 --> 42:56.820
Yes, sir.

905
42:58.050 --> 42:59.050
Pass on the order!

906
42:59.090 --> 43:00.740
The rear guard takes the lead.

907
43:00.740 --> 43:01.050
Attention!

908
43:01.050 --> 43:02.010
He keeps changing his mind by the hour.

909
43:02.010 --> 43:03.010
About face!

910
43:03.130 --> 43:03.770
Retreat!
